  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "id": "creating-a-custom-theme",
    "title": "Custom themes",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Use an installed built theme as the base for ordinary customization. Import it into your source and pass it as `extends` to `defineTheme({extends: importedTheme, ...})`. Build the result, then add the local slug. Only eject when you need to own and maintain a full source fork."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "A local theme is a folder in `src/themes/<slug>/` holding a `<name>Theme.ts` source that exports `<name>Theme`, and a same-stem `<name>Theme.doc.mjs` descriptor that `theme add` reads. The stem must be a valid export name, so a hyphenated slug drops the hyphen: `brand-dark` lives in `src/themes/brand-dark/brandDarkTheme.ts` exporting `brandDarkTheme`, beside `brandDarkTheme.doc.mjs`. The descriptor's `name` is the folder's slug, and it must declare its type or `theme add` and `theme list` refuse it. `astryx docs authoring theme-doc` lists every field."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "js",
        "code": "/** @type {import('@astryxdesign/cli/authoring').ThemeDoc} */\nexport default {\n  type: 'theme',\n  name: 'brand-dark',\n  displayName: 'Brand Dark',\n  description: 'The brand accent, tuned for dark mode.',\n  maintained: false,\n};",
        "label": "src/themes/brand-dark/brandDarkTheme.doc.mjs"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "bash",
        "code": "astryx theme list\nastryx theme add stone\nastryx theme eject stone\nastryx theme build src/themes/stone/stoneTheme.ts\nastryx theme add stone",
        "label": "Add to use, eject to fork"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "For an annotated map of the whole surface (every defineTheme field, the token families, and the component override syntax, each with the CLI command that prints its reference), run `astryx theme template`. It writes `theme.template.ts` into your project to read and copy from (`astryx init --features theme` writes it as part of project setup)."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "To apply a theme you created, see `astryx docs use-a-theme`. To generate colors from seed values, see the Palette section below. Before you eject a package theme instead, see when that fits in `astryx docs use-a-theme`."
      }
    ],
    "links": {
      "up": "astryx docs author-a-theme --index",
      "next": "astryx docs author-a-theme palette"
    }
  },
